Falsifies `file_allocation_table::table::verification::encoding_inverts_decoding`.

The defect: a bad-cluster entry encodes one past the marker, so the table stores an end-of-chain value and a bad cluster reads back as the end of a file.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(TableEntry::decode(file_allocation_table_type, raw), entry)`.

diff --git a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/table.rs b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/table.rs
--- a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/table.rs
+++ b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/table.rs
@@ -92,7 +92,7 @@ impl TableEntry {
             TableEntry::Free => 0,
             TableEntry::Reserved => 1,
             TableEntry::Next(next) => next & mask,
-            TableEntry::Bad => bad,
+            TableEntry::Bad => bad + 1,
             TableEntry::EndOfChain => mask,
         }
     }
